# KB Article Styling Rules
Use the styling best practices when writing/creating documents in this space.
## Active Voice vs Passive Voice
The documentation **_should always_** be in the active voice. Use the table to view examples of active vs. passive voice verb tenses, sentences, and more.

| Wording Tense | ✅ Active Voice | ❌ Passive Voice |
| ---| ---| --- |
| Simple Present | The Website Project Manager writes the SOP for website deployment. | The SOP for website deployment is written by the Website Project Manager. |
| Continuous Present | The development team is uploading the media assets to the staging site. | The media assets are being uploaded to the staging site by the development team. |
| Simple Past | The developer verified the reCAPTCHA v3 API keys yesterday. | The reCAPTCHA v3 API keys were verified by the QA engineer yesterday. |
| Continuous Past | The support desk was troubleshooting the DNS routing error all morning. | The DNS routing error was being troubleshooted by the support desk all morning. |
| Perfect Present | The technical writer has updated the onboarding documentation guidelines. | The onboarding documentation guidelines have been updated by the technical writer. |
| Perfect Past | The network administrator had resolved the server timeout before the site launch. | The server timeout had been resolved by the network administrator before the site launch. |
| Simple Future | The developer will configure the Elementor hamburger menu for mobile views. | The Elementor hamburger menu will be configured for mobile views by the developer. |
| Modals | You must click the 'Regenerate Files & Data' button to clear the CSS cache. | The 'Regenerate Files & Data' button must be clicked to clear the CSS cache. |

**_Style Note_**: While active voice is preferred for clarity, certain technical contexts may occasionally require passive phrasing. However, you should always default to an active structure when possible and ensure the chosen verb tense accurately reflects the operational step being described.